---
import rawData from '../../data/deployment-topics.json';
import TopicLayout from '../../components/TopicLayout.astro';
import ScoreBar from '../../components/ScoreBar.astro';
import { type DeploymentData, type DeploymentRow, auc, conditionLabel, intervalPct, modelLabel, pct } from '../../data/topics';

const data = rawData as unknown as DeploymentData;
const ssvep2 = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'mobile-ssvep-2s');
const ssvep5 = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'mobile-ssvep-5s');
const erp = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'mobile-erp');
const erpContrasts = data.paired_contrasts.filter(row => row.track === 'mobile-erp');
const conditions3 = ['standing','slow_walking','fast_walking'];
const conditions4 = [...conditions3,'slight_running'];
const ssvep2Models = ['author-cca','spectral-ridge','labram','cbramod'];
const ssvep5Models = ['author-cca','spectral-ridge'];
const rowFor = (rows: DeploymentRow[], model: string, condition: string, modality?: string) => rows.find(row => row.model === model && row.condition === condition && (modality ? row.modality === modality : true));
const ssvepCitation = data.dataset_citations.find(item => item.id === 'nemar-nm000125-v1.0.2');
const erpCitation = data.dataset_citations.find(item => item.id === 'nemar-nm000201-v1.0.2');
const contrastFor = (modality: string) => erpContrasts.find(row => row.modality === modality)!;
const signedAuc = (value: number) => `${value >= 0 ? '+' : '−'}${Math.abs(value).toFixed(3)} AUC`;
const runningChangeInterval = (interval: [number, number]) => `−${interval[1].toFixed(3)} to −${interval[0].toFixed(3)} AUC`;
---
<TopicLayout
  title="On the move"
  description="Motion robustness for mobile SSVEP and ERP decoding, with two- and five-second windows, scalp and ear channels, and balanced accuracy versus ROC AUC kept distinct."
  path="/topics/on-the-move/"
  eyebrow="Motion robustness · scalp and ear EEG"
  dek="Performance declines as participants move, but the size and meaning of that decline depend on the task, time window, electrode layout and metric. The two mobile derivatives come from one original study, so they are related evidence rather than independent replication cohorts."
  activeSlug="on-the-move"
>
  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="ssvep2-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Matched operating point</p><h2 id="ssvep2-heading">Two seconds, eight selected scalp channels</h2></div><p>The direct model comparison fixes the window at [0, 2 s), selects the same eight posterior scalp channels and evaluates 23 people on three SSVEP targets. Uniform chance is 33.3%.</p></div>
    <div class="topic-table scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Two-second mobile SSVEP results, scrolls horizontally">
      <table><caption>Participant-mean balanced accuracy; participant bootstrap 95% intervals are shown below each score.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th>{conditions3.map(condition => <th scope="col">{conditionLabel(condition)}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{ssvep2Models.map(model => <tr><th scope="row">{modelLabel(model)}<small>{model === 'author-cca' ? 'analytic reference' : model === 'spectral-ridge' ? 'trained on the other 22 standing participants' : 'frozen encoder + ridge, trained on other participants'}</small></th>{conditions3.map(condition => {
        const row = rowFor(ssvep2, model, condition)!;
        return <td><span class="metric">{pct(row.value)}</span><span class="interval">{intervalPct(row.confidence_interval_95)}</span><ScoreBar value={row.value} label={`${pct(row.value)} balanced accuracy`} tone={model === 'author-cca' ? 'rust' : model === 'spectral-ridge' ? 'olive' : 'ink'} /></td>;
      })}</tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p class="citation-note">Bars span 0–100%; chance is 33.3%.</p>
    <p class="protocol-note"><strong>Matched here means matched within this table.</strong> The foundation-model rows are fixed frozen-encoder adapters, not best fine-tuned results. LaBraM uses verified standard channel IDs; CBraMod uses an exploratory positional channel order. Record-level pretraining exposure is not certified.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="five-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A separate operating point</p><h2 id="five-heading">Five-second scalp and ear comparisons</h2></div><p>Longer windows and different electrode layouts change the problem. These classical five-second results do not share a ranking with the two-second foundation-model table above.</p></div>
    <div class="topic-table scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Five-second mobile SSVEP scalp and ear results, scrolls horizontally">
      <table><caption>Participant-mean balanced accuracy · 23 people · 3 targets. Scalp uses 8 selected channels from 32 recorded; ear uses 14 contacts.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Method / modality</th>{conditions3.map(condition => <th scope="col">{conditionLabel(condition)}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{['scalp','ear'].flatMap(modality => ssvep5Models.map(model => <tr><th scope="row">{modelLabel(model)}<small>{modality === 'scalp' ? '8 selected scalp channels' : '14 ear contacts'} · 5 s</small></th>{conditions3.map(condition => {
        const row = rowFor(ssvep5, model, condition, modality)!;
        return <td><span class="metric">{pct(row.value)}</span><span class="interval">{intervalPct(row.confidence_interval_95)}</span></td>;
      })}</tr>))}</tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="erp-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">ERP session transfer</p><h2 id="erp-heading">AUC falls toward chance while moving</h2></div><p>A separate temporal-feature L2 logistic regression is fit for each participant and modality on the first standing session, then used unchanged later. The endpoint is ROC AUC, not balanced accuracy.</p></div>
    <div class="finding">
      <div class="finding-number"><strong>{signedAuc(-contrastFor('scalp').difference)}</strong><span>Scalp ROC AUC change: standing to running, same 17 people</span></div>
      <div class="finding-copy"><h3>Use the paired common cohort for the running contrast</h3><p>Running contains 17 participants while standing and walking contain 24. Among the same 17 people, the standing-to-running change is {signedAuc(-contrastFor('scalp').difference)} for scalp and {signedAuc(-contrastFor('ear').difference)} for ear. Their descriptive 95% intervals are {runningChangeInterval(contrastFor('scalp').paired_participant_bootstrap_95)} and {runningChangeInterval(contrastFor('ear').paired_participant_bootstrap_95)}.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="topic-table scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Mobile ERP scalp and ear ROC AUC results, scrolls horizontally">
      <table><caption>Participant-mean ROC AUC. Scalp uses 32 channels; ear uses 14 contacts. Values in parentheses are participant bootstrap 95% intervals.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Modality</th>{conditions4.map(condition => <th scope="col">{conditionLabel(condition)}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{['scalp','ear'].map(modality => <tr><th scope="row">{modality === 'scalp' ? 'Scalp · 32 channels' : 'Ear · 14 contacts'}<small>standing-session fit · unchanged weights</small></th>{conditions4.map(condition => {
        const row = rowFor(erp, 'temporal-feature-logistic-regression', condition, modality)!;
        return <td><span class="metric">{auc(row.value)}</span><span class="interval">{row.confidence_interval_95 ? `${auc(row.confidence_interval_95[0])}–${auc(row.confidence_interval_95[1])}` : '—'}</span><small>n={row.participants}</small></td>;
      })}</tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" id="methods-and-limits" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Methods &amp; limits</p><h2 id="limits-heading">Four distinctions that keep the result honest</h2></div><p>Motion is the common theme, but the protocols answer different questions. No score is promoted into a cross-task leaderboard.</p></div>
    <div class="method-grid-wide">
      <article><h3>2 s stays separate from 5 s</h3><p>A longer analysis window can change decoding performance. The five-second classical results are an operating point, not a comparator for the two-second frozen encoders.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Scalp 8 is a selection</h3><p>The mobile SSVEP scalp view selects eight posterior channels from 32 recorded. It is not the native eight-channel wearable device used on the dry-versus-wet page.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Balanced accuracy differs from AUC</h3><p>The SSVEP endpoint is participant-mean balanced accuracy for a three-class task. The ERP endpoint is participant-mean ROC AUC. Their numeric values do not share a scale of practical meaning.</p></article>
      <article><h3>The derivatives share a study</h3><p>NEMAR nm000125 and nm000201 are SSVEP and ERP derivatives of the same original mobile BCI study, with different assessed sample counts.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="citation-list">
      {ssvepCitation && <article><h3>{ssvepCitation.identity.title}</h3><p>{ssvepCitation.identity.dataset_citation}</p><p>{ssvepCitation.identity.source_paper_citation}</p><p>NEMAR/MOABB-generated BIDS derivative · {ssvepCitation.identity.license}.</p><p><a href={ssvepCitation.primary_sources[0]} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SSVEP dataset ↗</a> · <a href={ssvepCitation.primary_sources[2]} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source study ↗</a></p></article>}
      {erpCitation && <article><h3>{erpCitation.identity.title}</h3><p>{erpCitation.identity.dataset_citation}</p><p>{erpCitation.identity.source_paper_citation}</p><p>NEMAR/MOABB-generated BIDS derivative · {erpCitation.identity.license}.</p><p><a href={erpCitation.primary_sources[0]} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ERP dataset ↗</a> · <a href={erpCitation.primary_sources[2]} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source study ↗</a></p></article>}
    </div>
    <p class="citation-note">Data source: <a href="/data/deployment-topics.json" download>reviewed aggregate JSON</a> · schema {data.schema_version} · generated {data.generated_at.slice(0,10)}.</p>
  </section>
</TopicLayout>
